{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_01U8oToZySK7ovPCPsWqMQht","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on the project documents and CLAUDE.md, here's what Anchor **is**:\n\n- **A single-user personal productivity system** for J.C. Liechty, living entirely in one folder (`C:\\dev\\Anchor`) with **plain markdown files as the source of truth** â€” no database, no syncing. Tasks/projects/inbox are tracked across domain files (academic, commercial, family, writing).\n\n- **It ships `anchor_gui.py`** (the declared deliverable): a self-contained, **stdlib-only Python HTTP server** that runs persistently as a Windows NSSM service on `http://localhost:8777`, generating an interactive browser dashboard that reads and writes the markdown directly. `anchor.py` is a CLI mirror of the same logic that also emits static `dashboard.html`.\n\n- **Core task layer:** a full task lifecycle (active â†’ done â†’ cancelled â†’ saved-for-later â†’ restored) with priorities, energy levels, due dates, notes, and per-domain views â€” editable live in the browser or via CLI commands.\n\n- **Its major recent thrust is an R&D \"Project Cockpit\" surface** (now at v4, built + merged to master 2026-06-13) that turns each project into a single-screen cockpit for **trio-driven R&D work** â€” the researchPrime â†’ Crucible â†’ Foreman skill trio. Each lane (Research/Planning/Build) shows its latest session as a **tile with one status light**; clicking expands an inline panel pairing a cached summary with a **real, resizable ConPTY terminal** (xterm.js over WebSocket), where launching a session feels like a normal Claude Code / Gemini session with the lane's skill auto-loading once.\n\n- **Engineering principles it holds to:** stdlib-only (one declared exception â€” optional `pywinpty` for the terminal subsystem, which degrades gracefully if absent), markdown-as-truth, everything human-readable/accessible from any CLI tool, and a **daily 5 AM self-test** (`anchor_healthcheck.py`) that exercises the v2/v3/v4 R&D surfaces fully stubbed (never the live service or real data).\n\n- **Branding:** presented as a **Ghost World Labs** tool \"powered by NextGen Nuclear â˜¢.\"\n\nThese claims are grounded in the locked North Stars (v3 \"mission control\" and v4 \"cockpit\"), the locked Stage-0/1 decisions (one ConPTY terminal substrate; skill-loads-once/greets-once), and the declared deliverable (`anchor_gui.py`)."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4410,"cache_read_input_tokens":45363,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":4410,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7de9593d-5aa8-4937-a93a-c5ea18dd75ba","uuid":"ad264bcd-455e-481c-b68c-9bab560e3201","request_id":"req_011Cc2Hjwqmfc1TfyDeyV54h"}
